Description: Say once per screen when its mode cannot be read
 Stereo::ScreenMode reads each screen's mode through KScreen and keeps a screen whose mode it cannot
 read as unknown, so a window there that shows an icon the theme has in stereo is drawn once, with
 the plain icon. When KScreen's read fails, the platform theme now says so once per screen in the
 log, naming the screen and KScreen's reason, instead of leaving the plain icons unexplained.
 The read is made once per program, when the first window that drew such an icon meets a screen.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
